      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to use the concept of inverse variation. When two variables are inversely proportional, their product remains constant. In this case, the force (F) required to loosen the bolt varies inversely with the length (L) of the handle. This relationship can be expressed as:\n\nF * L = k\n\nwhere k is a constant.\n\nFirst, let's find the value of k using the given values:\n\nF1 = 375 pounds\nL1 = 9 inches\n\nF1 * L1 = k\n375 * 9 = k\n3375 = k\n\nNow, we want to find the force (F2) required when the length of the handle (L2) is 15 inches. We can use the same constant (k) to find F2:\n\nF2 * L2 = k\nF2 * 15 = 3375\n\nTo find F2, divide both sides by 15:\n\nF2 = 3375 / 15\nF2 = 225\n\nSo, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require 225 pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
