      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let the force required to loosen the bolt be \\( F \\) and the handle length be \\( L \\). According to the problem, \\( F \\) varies inversely with \\( L \\), which means \\( F \\times L = k \\), where \\( k \\) is a constant.\n\nFirst, we need to find the constant \\( k \\). We know that when \\( L = 9 \\) inches, \\( F = 375 \\) pounds. So, we can write:\n\\[ 375 \\times 9 = k \\]\n\\[ k = 3375 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the force \\( F \\) required when \\( L = 15 \\) inches. Using the constant \\( k \\), we can write:\n\\[ F \\times 15 = 3375 \\]\n\\[ F = \\frac{3375}{15} \\]\n\\[ F = 225 \\]\n\nTherefore, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require \\(\\boxed{225}\\) pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
