      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we can use the concept of inverse variation. In inverse variation, the product of two variables is constant. In this case, the force (F) and the handle length (L) are inversely proportional, so we can write the equation as:\n\nF * L = k\n\nwhere k is the constant of proportionality.\n\nFirst, we need to find the value of k using the given data. We know that a wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force to loosen a certain bolt. So, we can write:\n\n375 * 9 = k\n\nNow, we can solve for k:\n\n375 * 9 = 3375\n\nSo, the constant of proportionality (k) is 3375.\n\nNext, we need to find the force required for a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches. We can use the same equation:\n\nF * 15 = 3375\n\nNow, we can solve for F:\n\nF = 3375 / 15\n\nF = 225\n\nTherefore, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require 225 pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
