      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The force needed to loosen a bolt varies inversely with the length of the handle of the wrench used. This means that the product of the force and the handle length is a constant value. Let's denote this constant value by \\( k \\).\n\nGiven that a wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force, we can write:\n\\[ k = 9 \\times 375 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the force required when the handle length is 15 inches. Let's denote this force by \\( F \\). Using the inverse relationship, we have:\n\\[ k = 15 \\times F \\]\n\nSince \\( k \\) is the same in both cases, we can set the two expressions for \\( k \\) equal to each other:\n\\[ 9 \\times 375 = 15 \\times F \\]\n\nSolving for \\( F \\):\n\\[ 3375 = 15 \\times F \\]\n\\[ F = \\frac{3375}{15} \\]\n\\[ F = 225 \\]\n\nTherefore, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require \\boxed{225} pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
